<http://data.silknow.org/object/576ff960-b7cf-3a71-a3d1-f1e6df08a451>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Textile panel of silk, France, 1750-1775"@en , "Textile panel of silk woven with a ground in off-white silk divided into squares, alternating in plain tabby and ribbed with a white silk flushing warp. In the alternate plain square there is a small floral sprig in green, red and yellow silk.\n\nCannellé ground with additional warp threads floating over seven shoots and bound by the eighth. The coloured sprigs are made by pattern wefts and the white centre of each coloured sprig is formed by the flushing warp. Lined with net and edged with buff silk braid."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/016e3970-2cb7-39ec-a73d-f649c18942ef> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Textile panel of silk woven with a ground in off-white silk divided into squares, alternating in plain tabby and ribbed with a white silk flushing warp. In the alternate plain square there is a small floral sprig in green, red and yellow silk.\n\nCannellé ground with additional warp threads floating over seven shoots and bound by the eighth. The coloured sprigs are made by pattern wefts and the white centre of each coloured sprig is formed by the flushing warp. Lined with net and edged with buff silk braid."@en , "Textile panel of silk, France, 1750-1775"@en ;
